  "published": "1900-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.3.0: Scene, persistence and input overhaul (contains breaking changes). Scene switching is now destructive and centralized in SceneManager.Load: the current scene is torn down and the next built fresh, removing the double/triple OnClose and the surprising side-effecting Scene.Current setter (Scene.Current is now a plain property). Added cross-scene persistence via the [Persistent] field attribute (one shared instance per component type, started once, spared from teardown, with field write-back), reachable through SceneManager.GetPersistentComponent<T>(). Added the [Detached] field attribute to opt a component field out of automatic discovery, and a cycle guard to the field scan. Input bindings are now two-tier: BindAction is scene-scoped and cleared on every switch, while the new BindGlobalAction overloads survive switches; InvokeActions iterates a snapshot so a binding that switches scenes can no longer corrupt the enumeration. BREAKING: removed the unused SceneManager scene registry APIs (RemoveScene, GetScene, GetRequiredScene, GetAllScenes). Also fixes Draw shared shapes inheriting rotation/outline/fill from a previous draw (options are now applied unconditionally with explicit fallbacks). Drawing ergonomics: added Draw.Clear(color) which clears the window Draw actually renders to (correct under SetDrawingWindow redirects), an implicit Color-to-DrawOptions/TextDrawOptions conversion so a color can be passed straight to a draw call, and a fluent DrawOptions builder (DrawOptions.Fill/Outline/Rotated plus WithFill/WithOutline/WithRotation/WithOpacity).",
